invariant: INV-58
file: srv_auth.c
catches: srv_auth_test
reason: sign_ecdsa fills the noise with a constant instead of a draw, so
  the server signs one transcript the same way every time, and the hedge
  is gone. Every signature still verifies. bin/srv_auth_test signs one
  transcript twice and requires two signatures, and requires the first to
  be p256_sign_hedged's over the noise the hook wrote.

--- old
    rand_draw(cfg, noise, sizeof noise);
--- new
    memset(noise, 1, sizeof noise);
